  "domain": "infrastructure",
  "definition": "An Operating System (OS) is the foundational software layer that manages hardware resources \u2014 CPU scheduling, memory allocation, file systems, device drivers, and process isolation \u2014 and provides a stable interface for application software. In spatial computing and XR contexts, OS-level capabilities such as real-time scheduling, GPU access, and sensor integration are critical; specialised spatial OSes must coordinate head-tracking, display refresh, and input fusion at sub-millisecond latencies.",
